    "title": "otosora v0.8.5",
    "notes": "# Otosora 0.8.5\n\n## Streaming\n- One song YouTube won't play no longer stops every other song. YouTube asks for a sign-in on some uploads, and Otosora used to treat that as the whole network being blocked: it paused all streaming for two minutes and the queue skipped from song to song.\n- That song is now skipped on its own, and a message names it and says why: sign-in required, age-restricted, private, removed, or not available in your country. Another version of the song often plays fine.\n- Errors say what went wrong. \"Check the connection\" now shows only when YouTube really couldn't be reached.\n- A stream that stops answering gives up after 20 seconds instead of loading forever. On Windows and Linux, a stuck song lookup stops after 90 seconds.\n- A wrong size guess for some streams no longer cuts songs short or leaves them hanging at the end.\n",
    "publishedAt": "2026-11-07T21:40:37Z",
